Development lead-based paint hazard control grant program: study method</article-title><source>Environ Res</source><volume>98</volume><fpage>315</fpage><lpage>328</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15910786</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b6-ehp-117-a332"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Galke</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Clark</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Wilson</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Jacobs</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Succop</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Dixon</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2001</year><article-title>Evaluation of the HUD Lead Hazard Control grant program: early overall findings</article-title><source>Environ Res</source><volume>86</volume><fpage>149</fpage><lpage>156</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11437461</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b7-ehp-117-a332"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Glass</surname><given-names>TA</given-names></name><name><surname>Bandeen-Roche</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>McAtee</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Bolla</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Todd</surname><given-names>AC</given-names></name><name><surname>Schwartz</surname><given-names>BS</given-names></name></person-group><year>2009</year><article-title>Neighborhood psychosocial hazards and the association of cumulative lead dose with cognitive function in older adults</article-title><source>Am J Epidemiol</source><volume>169</volume><issue>6</issue><fpage>683</fpage><lpage>692</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">19155330</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b8-ehp-117-a332"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-t